{"resourceIdentifier":"3741","resourceName":"Mudurnu Biogas Energy Power Plant","description":"Mudurnu Biogas Power Plant, built and operated in Bolu Province, Mudurnu District, Pelitözü Village has an installed capacity of 2.4 MWe/ 2.464 MWm. as per the generation licence. The purpose of the project activity is to produce electricity from poultry and cattle manure with biomethanization process which will also result in fermented products that could be utilized as fertilizers by local farmers. Mudurnu Biogas Power plant has been granted the generation license from EMRA on 30/07/2020. As per the generation license, the annual expected generation is 18,480 MWh/year. As per the generation licence, the facility is expected to generate 18,480 MWh/year. The facility is also expected to generate 7,761,725 m3/year (21,265 m3/day) biogas. It is estimated that the project help reduce the carbon emissions by an average of 90,699.07 tons annually. The average total emission reduction for the whole crediting period is calculated as 634,894 t CO2e. The project activity has been connected to the national grid by Mudurnu - Cuma KÖK Energy Transmission Line Mudurnu Medium Voltage Transformer Station.","location":{"latitude":40.515667,"longitude":31.261559},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-11-25","endExclusive":"2022-12-26","endInclusive":"2022-12-25"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3741"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Mudurnu Enerji Sanayi ve Tcaret A.Ş."},{"type":"string","value":"Bolu, Turkey"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"90699"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"st